course: dictionary
lesson: 3629
title: Finely: small, careful and exact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: "Finely" is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. It can mean in very small or thin pieces, as in «finely chopped onion». Picture a cook with a sharp knife making tiny, thin bits.
explain: It can also mean very carefully and exactly, with small details. A «finely balanced» game is so evenly matched that either side could win, and «finely tuned» means adjusted with great care so it works exactly right.
explain: Look at the words around it. Food words point to small pieces, while words like «tuned» or «balanced» point to exact care or a close match. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Finely means in very small or thin pieces, or very carefully and exactly.
fact: «Finely chopped» means cut into tiny pieces, as recipes often ask.
fact: «Finely balanced» means so evenly matched that the result is very close.
fact: «Finely tuned» means adjusted with great care so that it works exactly right.
fact: In old or formal writing, finely can mean in a fine, beautiful way.
exercise: Recipe: «Add one finely chopped onion.» What does finely mean here? | In a fine, beautiful way | *In very small pieces | Slowly, on the stove | Very quickly and loudly
exercise: «The two teams were finely balanced all game.» What does this suggest? | *They were very evenly matched | One team was far ahead all game | The players were bored | The game was cancelled
exercise: In «The mantis shrimp sees colours fast rather than finely», what does finely mean? | *With fine, careful detail | Without any colour | Very loudly | In a thin, wiggly line
test: «The engine was finely tuned so it ran smoothly.» What does finely tuned mean? | *Adjusted with great care to work exactly right | Broken into small pieces | Painted in fine colours | Left out in the rain
test: Which phrase means cut into tiny pieces? | Slowly tuned | Finely balanced | Loudly shouted | *Finely chopped
exam: Which word fits best in «The watchmaker worked ___ on the tiny gears.»? | *Finely | Loudly | Gently | Roughly
